@PaymentProvider_HostAddress = http://localhost:5103
@ApiKey = demo-provider-key

### Start the AppHost first. The payment provider is a stand-in for an outside provider.
### It knows its caller by the API key, which is a bearer token. The AppHost passes the same key to Orders.
### The Idempotency-Key header is the id of the saga. The same key is charged once and always gets the same answer.
### The failures are settings of the service, not of a call. See the demo readme, chapter Payment service.

### Charge => OK, approved (an amount up to 500 euro)
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/charges HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{ApiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9001",
  "amount": 42.50
}

### Charge => OK, the same answer and the same reference as above, and nothing is charged again
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/charges HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{ApiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9001",
  "amount": 42.50
}

### Charge => OK, declined (an amount above 500 euro). A decline is an answer, not an error.
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/charges HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{ApiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009002
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9002",
  "amount": 500.01
}

### Charge => Bad request, no order number and no amount
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/charges HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{ApiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009003
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "",
  "amount": 0
}

### Charge => Unauthorized, a wrong API key
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/charges HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer not-the-key
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009004
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9004",
  "amount": 10
}

### Refund => OK, refunded (the first charge above was approved)
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/refunds HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{ApiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009011
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9001"
}

### Refund => OK, nothing_to_refund (the second charge was declined)
POST {{PaymentProvider_HostAddress}}/refunds HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{ApiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 3f4d6a30-0000-4000-8000-000000009012
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderNumber": "20261106-9002"
}
